const prompt="Use case: stylized-concept. Create a NEW production raster tree atlas, 4 columns x 2 rows, eight isolated tree sprites. Input image is ONLY the user's exact minimal game-style reference. STRICT MINIMALISM: every tree is composed of only TWO OR THREE LARGE SOLID COLOR SHAPES for its entire crown, plus one very short plain brown trunk. No small leaf lobes, no tiny scallops, no leaf dots, no flecks, no branches, no root details. Extremely simple flat cut-paper-like matte silhouettes, NOT a detailed painterly tree. Row1 four broadleaf silhouette variants: simple round crown with 5–7 big organic lobes, simple wider crown, simple oval crown, simple asymmetric two-mass crown. Row2 four pine silhouettes: compact 3 broad-layer fir, wider 3-layer fir, slim simple 3-layer pine, uneven 3-layer pine. Each conifer layer is one big uncomplicated gently lobed shape, never fringed with many notches. CRITICAL COLORS AND CONTRAST: medium olive main canopy approximately #737b38, modest darker olive #626c35, modest lighter olive #848d45. No cream or yellow highlights, no near-black patches, no extreme contrast. Choose ONE large shadow plane lower left and ONE modest lit plane upper right, nothing else. Camera orthographic nearly straight overhead 15 degrees FROM VERTICAL, no side rotation, no perspective; crown tops dominant and front/trunk very short. Background truly transparent, no haze no glow no gradient no noise no scene no ground tiles no presentation lighting. If using contact shadow it is tiny and flat, never a broad blurred halo. Full object within its cell with generous empty margins, consistent scale and base alignment. No labels text grid borders. These should resemble the user's original uncomplicated trees, even simpler, with variation in silhouette rather than embellishment.";
store("treeprompt3",prompt);const r=await tools.image_gen__imagegen({prompt,referenced_image_paths:["/home/suselman/projects/hearthvale/docs/references/style-world.jpg"],transparent_background:true});store("treegen3",r);if(r.output_hint)text(r.output_hint);

