const prompt="Use case: stylized-concept. Generate a NEW production game resource sprite atlas, exactly 4 columns x 2 rows. Reference image 1 is specifically the VOLUME and ORGANIC BROKEN STONE SHAPES reference, not its pixel-art style; reference image 2 is our minimal flat earthy game art style. Top row four distinct ordinary stone GROUPS; bottom row the same four broad shape families with small golden veins/inclusions in the stone. Main requirement: stones must have convincing THREE-DIMENSIONAL FORM despite using simple flat colors: different heights, irregular broad top plateaus, stepped chipped ledges and a SHORT clearly distinct darker vertical front rim. Not flat painted blobs, not low-poly triangular hemispheres, not tall front-view pyramids. Variant1 one squat irregular layered boulder with one smaller stone; variant2 three uneven interlocking squat stones at different heights; variant3 wider low cluster with a raised stepped top stone; variant4 asymmetrical two-level rocky outcrop with a few tiny rubble pieces. Each pile only 3–4 LARGE color planes, warm gray-taupe/ochre-gray, cream warm upper-right top planes and muted darker short lower-left/front faces. Minimal detail, no mesh triangle facets, no noise, no glossy gradients. Camera RULE orthographic nearly directly overhead, exactly 15 degrees FROM VERTICAL, straight from front, no side rotation, no perspective narrowing. Show dominant irregular top footprint and short height extrusion, like the reference stones viewed from above. Light upper RIGHT. Every pile has a MANDATORY VISIBLE COMPACT FLAT ground shadow cast towards LOWER LEFT, extending outside the stone outline 20–30% of its width, muted dark olive (#56613a), never blurry or glowing. Gold in bottom row: 2–3 short muted gold vein streaks/flecks, not all-yellow rocks. All sprites centered in own equal cell, fully contained including shadow with generous transparent margins. Actual empty transparent background, opaque solid object interiors. No text, labels, frame, grid, scenery, ground tiles or presentation background.";
store("rockvolumeprompt",prompt);const r=await tools.image_gen__imagegen({prompt,referenced_image_paths:["/home/suselman/projects/hearthvale/docs/references/stone-volume.jpg","/home/suselman/projects/hearthvale/docs/references/style-world.jpg"],transparent_background:true});store("rockvolumegen",r);if(r.output_hint)text(r.output_hint);

